Neovim colorscheme for {{ theme.name }}. {{ theme.description }}

## Installation

{% if adapter.mirror -%}
### lazy.nvim

```lua
{
    "{{ adapter.mirror }}",
    config = function()
        require("{{ theme.id }}").setup({ variant = "{{ first.variant.id }}" })
        vim.cmd.colorscheme("{{ theme.id }}")
    end,
}
```

To pin a specific version:

```lua
{
    "{{ adapter.mirror }}",
    tag = "v0.9.0",
    config = function()
        require("{{ theme.id }}").setup({ variant = "{{ first.variant.id }}" })
        vim.cmd.colorscheme("{{ theme.id }}")
    end,
}
```

### vim-plug

```vim
Plug '{{ adapter.mirror }}'
```

Then in your config:

```lua
lua require("{{ theme.id }}").setup({ variant = "{{ first.variant.id }}" })
colorscheme {{ theme.id }}
```

### dein.vim

```vim
call dein#add('{{ adapter.mirror }}')
```

Then in your config:

```lua
lua require("{{ theme.id }}").setup({ variant = "{{ first.variant.id }}" })
colorscheme {{ theme.id }}
```
{% else -%}
### lazy.nvim

Point lazy.nvim at this directory:

```lua
{
    dir = "/path/to/this/directory",
    config = function()
        require("{{ theme.id }}").setup({ variant = "{{ first.variant.id }}" })
        vim.cmd.colorscheme("{{ theme.id }}")
    end,
}
```
{% endif %}
